1. modify the HOME macro in make.inc to point to where crd-fasteig is installed
2. Define the locations of 
   MKL
   eigen
3. Set compiler and compiler flags
Then do
make lib 
to generate a libfasteig_$(PLAT).a where PLAT is a user defined Platform name, e.g., Perlmutter
## Perlmutter notes (MKL vs Eigen)
By default, `make.inc` enables Eigen's MKL integration (`-DEIGEN_USE_MKL_ALL`) and links MKL.
To build **without** MKL/Pardiso (use Eigen's own sparse factorization), override `USE_MKL` and
avoid linking MKL when building examples:
make -C src clean
make -C src MAKEINC=../make.inc USE_MKL=""
make -C examples clean
make -C examples MAKEINC=../make.inc USE_MKL="" MKL=""
When running a generalized problem, the log will print the factorization backend:
  - `MKL PardisoLDLT` (MKL enabled)
  - `Eigen SimplicialLDLT` (MKL disabled)
To run some examples
cd examples
make
generates a CPU executable called 'runfasteig_cpu'. With CUDA enabled
(`make USE_CUDA=1` and `make -C examples USE_CUDA=1`), the examples build
also generates 'runfasteig_gpu'.
Run the executable by the following command
./runfasteig_cpu  SiO.input
For the executor-aware solvers, the CPU and GPU executables use the same input
deck. Keep the solver name in the input file and select the backend by
executable, for example:
./runfasteig_cpu  SiO.input
./runfasteig_gpu  SiO.input
The GPU executable dispatches `Lanczos`, `BlockLanczos`, `KrylovSchur`,
`BlockKrylovSchur`, and `Davidson` through the CUDA executor. These CUDA
paths currently support standard stored-matrix problems; generalized
Krylov--Schur remains host-only.
CUDA `which SAI` is available for scalar Lanczos and Krylov--Schur and requires
NVIDIA cuDSS. The block methods and Davidson do not support `SAI`.
### Optional project-space cuDSS install
If your system does not provide a cuDSS module, install cuDSS into the checkout:
```
tools/install_cudss.sh
make -C examples USE_CUDA=1
```
If pip cannot download cuDSS, download the Linux cuDSS archive from
NVIDIA and extract it with:
```
tools/install_cudss.sh --tarball /path/to/cudss-linux-*.tar.*
make -C examples USE_CUDA=1
```
The default makefile checks for the checkout-local install automatically. On
Perlmutter, a shared project-space install such as
`/global/cfs/cdirs/m1027/Dong/cudss` is also auto-detected when the checkout is
under `/global/cfs/cdirs/m1027/Dong/`. For any other custom cuDSS location,
source the generated `cudss-env.sh` or pass `CUDSS_PATH` and `CUDSS_LIBDIR`
explicitly.
where SiO.input is an input file that contains a list of problem descriptions
amatrix ./Sparse_Matrices/SiO.mtx
logfile SiO
nev     5
which   SR
solver  Chebyshev
maxiter 10
maxdim  20
degree  8
tol     1e-6

